00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:29.480
<i>If he wins the next point, it'll be love-40.</i>

00:13:29.480 --> 00:13:30.990
<i>I'm out of chances.</i>

00:13:31.640 --> 00:13:39.310
Pressure           Pressure           Pressure

00:13:32.590 --> 00:13:34.510
<i>40% didn't work.</i>

00:13:35.060 --> 00:13:38.520
<i>My intuition tells me 20-30% would be best.</i>

00:13:39.310 --> 00:13:52.640
Pressure

00:13:39.370 --> 00:13:42.240
<i>But the size of the pressure 
changes every time.</i>

00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:45.390
<i>Even worse, it's grown to a size 
I've never experienced before,</i>

00:13:45.390 --> 00:13:47.410
<i>so I don't know exactly how big it is.</i>

00:13:48.300 --> 00:13:52.640
<i>There's no way I can accurately 
judge the size of my pressure!</i>

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:54.390
Fifteen seconds.

00:13:54.820 --> 00:13:57.080
<i>He's thinking about something again.</i>

00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:58.650
<i>I've gotta be careful when that happens.</i>

00:13:59.050 --> 00:14:01.570
<i>Visualize the causes of my pressure,</i>

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:05.900
Pressure

00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:04.100
<i>then imagine erasing it,</i>

00:14:04.590 --> 00:14:05.900
<i>leaving just a little.</i>

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:11.030
<i>That was fast!</i>

00:14:11.780 --> 00:14:12.780
<i>It's working!</i>

00:14:16.700 --> 00:14:18.420
15-30.

00:14:19.380 --> 00:14:20.170
Yes!

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:21.540
Yes!

00:14:21.890 --> 00:14:24.800
<i>Good! That definitely went well!</i>

00:14:25.370 --> 00:14:26.630
<i>It'll work!</i>

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:30.640
<i>It's best to leave 20-30% 
of my pressure unerased!</i>

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:35.650
I'm so nervous, I think I'll 
fall over before he does.

00:14:35.650 --> 00:14:38.640
Yeah, we know his future's riding on this.

00:14:39.070 --> 00:14:41.900
Now that he's come this far, 
I want to give him the win!

00:14:42.130 --> 00:14:44.870
Today's a little different from usual.

00:14:46.080 --> 00:14:51.410
Usually, Yosshi's opponent in a close 
match would start to freak out by now.

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:53.050
But Maruo-kun is...

00:14:53.050 --> 00:14:55.910
Idiot! If that's what you think, 
cheer for him more!

00:14:56.280 --> 00:14:59.100
Yosshi! This is it!

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:00.240
Win this one, and you've got break point!

00:15:00.240 --> 00:15:01.420
Yosshi!

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:03.790
Come on... Come on... Come on...

00:15:06.050 --> 00:15:08.870
<i>I've figured out how to play strong</i>

00:15:08.870 --> 00:15:12.250
<i>in a high-pressure situation like this.</i>

00:15:12.250 --> 00:15:14.880
<i>All that's left is to believe 
in myself and find out</i>

00:15:15.450 --> 00:15:18.060
<i>how well I can see it through.</i>

00:15:18.840 --> 00:15:20.190
<i>I'll conquer myself</i>

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:21.940
<i>and Ide-kun!</i>

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:26.700
<i>Visualize erasing all but 
20-30% of the pressure.</i>

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:29.580
<i>Once I feel the excess tension draining,</i>

00:15:29.580 --> 00:15:30.700
<i>focus!</i>

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:38.850
30-all.

00:15:38.850 --> 00:15:40.080
Yes!

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:43.480
<i>I was right. It's working really well!</i>

00:15:44.120 --> 00:15:45.840
<i>Now just stay focused!</i>

00:15:46.380 --> 00:15:49.270
Maruo came back from love-30.

00:15:49.270 --> 00:15:51.840
There's really no telling how this will end.

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:55.100
<i>It's coming crosscourt!</i>

00:15:58.720 --> 00:16:00.050
40-30.

00:16:01.610 --> 00:16:02.980
<i>This feeling...</i>

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:04.630
<i>I've felt it before.</i>

00:16:08.450 --> 00:16:09.740
Game: Maruo.

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:12.610
Score: 6-5. Final set.

00:16:14.770 --> 00:16:16.050
Seriously?!

00:16:16.050 --> 00:16:18.620
Ide! You've gotta hold!

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:22.760
All right! Way to hold serve!

00:16:22.760 --> 00:16:24.970
Holding on here made a big difference!

00:16:24.970 --> 00:16:27.940
If he takes the next game, he wins, right?

00:16:27.940 --> 00:16:30.630
<i>If you can keep the pressure under control,</i>

00:16:30.940 --> 00:16:33.130
<i>you can beat Ide for sure!</i>

00:16:34.410 --> 00:16:35.620
<i>That's right.</i>

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:37.930
<i>It was when I played Alex in Florida,</i>

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:40.930
<i>and in my match with Araya-kun, too.</i>

00:16:40.930 --> 00:16:43.010
<i>I found a balance between 
my reason and instinct,</i>

00:16:43.010 --> 00:16:44.790
<i>and I was able to play really well.</i>

00:16:45.410 --> 00:16:49.750
<i>So as I used my reason to visualize the 
pressure and played instinctively,</i>

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:52.230
<i>I stumbled across that perfect balance?</i>

00:16:52.680 --> 00:16:55.130
<i>Then if I can keep this up,</i>

00:16:55.130 --> 00:16:57.220
<i>even just for this next game...</i>

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:00.390
<i>The next game is critical.</i>

00:17:00.390 --> 00:17:03.160
<i>But if I can overcome it, I can win.</i>

00:17:03.670 --> 00:17:07.170
<i>So, guys, lend me even more 
of your strength now.</i>

00:17:07.510 --> 00:17:10.910
<i>The more people expect from 
me, the stronger I become!</i>

00:17:11.820 --> 00:17:15.930
<i>I'm going to use this strength 
I have to make everyone smile!</i>

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:18.780
Time.

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:24.770
<i>To break his serve and win,</i>

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:27.060
<i>I need to stay in the same 
state as the previous game.</i>

00:17:27.530 --> 00:17:31.130
<i>Like before, once play begins, 
focus on Ide-kun,</i>

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:34.150
<i>and leave the rest to my instincts!</i>

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:35.300
<i>Center!</i>

00:17:37.460 --> 00:17:38.780
Love-15.

00:17:39.690 --> 00:17:40.840
Yes!

00:17:40.840 --> 00:17:42.540
<i>I'm still in the right state!</i>

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:44.790
<i>As far as I'm concerned,</i>

00:17:45.340 --> 00:17:47.290
<i>this doesn't count as a crisis just yet!</i>

00:17:53.460 --> 00:17:55.010
A drop shot, now?

00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:56.520
Maruo-kun is moving up.

00:17:56.520 --> 00:17:57.470
Here comes Ide, too.

00:17:58.220 --> 00:17:58.970
<i>Get there!</i>

00:18:05.230 --> 00:18:06.420
<i>No, you don't!</i>

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:14.180
Love-30.

00:18:15.870 --> 00:18:17.450
What was that?! It was awesome!

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:18.870
He hit it between his legs!

00:18:18.870 --> 00:18:20.710
That actually happens?!

00:18:20.710 --> 00:18:22.910
It was the only way to return that shot!

00:18:23.980 --> 00:18:24.910
Are you serious?

00:18:28.810 --> 00:18:29.920
<i>If I'm</i>

00:18:30.270 --> 00:18:32.670
<i>going to win consecutive 
points, it has to be here!</i>

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:35.660
<i>Interesting!</i>

00:18:37.140 --> 00:18:39.050
<i>Crap! Too weak? Where will he hit it?</i>

00:18:42.430 --> 00:18:43.430
<i>Another drop shot?!</i>

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:48.870
15-30.

00:18:50.190 --> 00:18:54.370
Whoa, whoa! A hit between the legs and 
consecutive drop shots, at a time like this?

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:56.200
What's going on in this match?

00:18:56.200 --> 00:19:00.200
And they actually worked. 
Those two are not normal right now.

00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:04.450
Who'd keep at it after shots like 
that were just returned against them?

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:05.520
Yes!

00:19:05.520 --> 00:19:06.430
That's it, Ide!

00:19:06.430 --> 00:19:08.040
If he gets you, get him back!

00:19:08.290 --> 00:19:09.650
<i>No.</i>

00:19:09.650 --> 00:19:12.070
<i>He surprised me with the 
consecutive drop shots,</i>

00:19:12.070 --> 00:19:14.270
<i>but my return before that was no good.</i>

00:19:15.070 --> 00:19:16.840
<i>Telling myself before play began</i>

00:19:16.840 --> 00:19:19.010
<i>that two more points would get me the win</i>

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:20.420
<i>just put more pressure on me.</i>

00:19:21.300 --> 00:19:25.370
<i>Every time the situation changes, 
I have to confront myself.</i>

00:19:25.370 --> 00:19:28.730
<i>Visualize all the pressure in my head,</i>

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:30.440
<i>then erase it, leaving just a bit.</i>

00:19:31.510 --> 00:19:36.400
<i>I'm not sure why, but repeating that 
cycle put me in my best state!</i>

00:19:36.830 --> 00:19:41.150
<i>So I'll do my best to repeat 
that again from the beginning.</i>

00:19:41.370 --> 00:19:42.960
<i>It's my only chance!</i>

00:19:42.960 --> 00:19:45.870
<i>That's everything I can do right now!</i>

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:03.510
15-40.

00:20:04.280 --> 00:20:05.730
Match point!

00:20:05.730 --> 00:20:08.010
Maruo got to match point first!

00:20:08.010 --> 00:20:10.360
Ei-chan! Finish it here!

00:20:10.360 --> 00:20:12.020
Maruo-kun, you can do it!

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:15.270
You're kidding me! Ide's gonna 
lose a match like this?!

00:20:15.270 --> 00:20:17.450
We don't know that yet!

00:20:16.250 --> 00:20:18.780
Come on... Onii-chan, come on!

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:20.160
Hang in there, Yosshi!

00:20:20.160 --> 00:20:21.010
Yosshi!

00:20:21.010 --> 00:20:22.280
You're just getting started!

00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:26.030
Even as a spectator, 
match point is an awful thing.

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:32.880
But the one who shows his utmost strength 
when he's backed against the wall like this

00:20:33.560 --> 00:20:35.090
is the man named Ide.

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:57.310
30-40.

00:21:55.580 --> 00:21:57.280
Game, set, and match.

00:21:57.280 --> 00:21:58.710
Winner: Maruo.

00:21:58.710 --> 00:22:02.770
Score: 6-2, 3-6, 7-5.

00:21:59.780 --> 00:22:03.720
Incredible! Maruo actually won 
a close match against Ide!

00:22:03.720 --> 00:22:05.420
You both did great!

00:22:05.420 --> 00:22:07.050
I really got excited!

00:22:07.050 --> 00:22:08.720
That was so fun to watch!

00:22:08.720 --> 00:22:12.220
Maruo Eiichiro 
Ide Yoshiaki

00:22:10.120 --> 00:22:11.200
<i>I won!</i>

00:22:12.220 --> 00:22:15.180
Ide! You really are the best!

00:22:13.890 --> 00:22:16.200
Damn...

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:17.230
Even when you lose, you look awesome!

00:22:16.200 --> 00:22:17.230
But, hey...

00:22:17.750 --> 00:22:20.730
That was the best match ever, 
so I guess it's all good.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:25.020
Next Time

00:24:00.520 --> 00:24:02.150
That was a great match against Ide.

00:24:02.150 --> 00:24:05.250
I was able to calm down after 
I noticed you were there.

00:24:05.250 --> 00:24:06.420
Oh, right...

00:24:06.420 --> 00:24:08.810
This is Takagi Sakuya. He's from my club.

00:24:08.810 --> 00:24:11.860
I thought I should introduce you, 
since you might end up playing him.

00:24:11.860 --> 00:24:14.340
This is the fourth seed, Takagi Sakuya?

00:24:14.680 --> 00:24:17.110
So he and Nabae-kun are friends...

00:24:17.110 --> 00:24:21.090
Wait, he didn't even introduce 
himself? What's with him?

00:24:21.090 --> 00:24:22.870
Next time on <i>Baby Steps</i>,

00:24:21.540 --> 00:24:25.020
A Rude First Meeting

00:24:22.870 --> 00:24:24.450
"A Rude First Meeting."

00:24:25.210 --> 00:24:30.500
End
